  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 249 AM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nClear skies overnight, but cloud cover streaming southwards out\nof northern Minnesota will lead to a mostly cloudy morning &\nafternoon. Northwest winds increase through the morning with\nwind gusts of 20-25 mph expected through sunset. Cyclonic flow &\ncold advection aloft will result in prime conditions for widely\nscattered dirunally-driven rain showers to develop this\nafternoon, although the drought conditions may limit how much\nprecip we actually see. Best chances for a brief rain shower\nthis afternoon will be across western Wisconsin.\n\nHigh pressure holds over the region through Friday leading to\ncontinued dry conditions with seasonable temperatures. A more \nactive upper air pattern develops over the weekend as the jet \nstream strengthens along the US- Canada border & a number of \nshortwaves traverse through the Upper Midwest. These look to be \nrelatively weak over the weekend, but supportive of at least \nscattered thunderstorm chances. The best chance for rain this \nweekend looks to be overnight Friday night into Saturday \nmorning. A stronger wave looks possible early next week, but \nstill low confidence on the track/timing & location of the \nheaviest rain potential.",
